# BUG-614: a call in this statement skipped every front-end check -- `checkStmt1` had no arm
# for it (it fell to `else pass`) -- so `"s".count()`, which needs one argument, passed
# `zebra -c` and failed inside zig or panicked at run time. Found by Fable as an `assert`
# whose `and` operand called `.count()` where `.len` was meant.

def main()
    var s = "hello"
    var c = 0
    c <<- s.count()
    print(c)
